# Proposed by an executor (2026-10-15); the documenter may edit or drop it.
# Story: a laptop beside a monitor, nothing docked, the browser on the laptop, mail on the monitor. The lid is shut for the
# day; in the evening the laptop goes along alone; next morning the monitor is plugged in again. Everything is where it was.
# Arbor used to take the browser off the laptop and put it on the monitor, which had only had it to visit while the lid
# was shut.
# Played as hosted Macs were recorded: macOS's list of displays is new at once, the apps say where macOS has taken their
# windows, and Arbor is told once the displays have settled.
# Reference: rule 2 (nothing moves until the person docks something), Q20 (there and back is nothing), F08.
plug side right 1920x1080
open Browser 1000x600
open Mail 700x500
move 101 60 65 1000 600
move 102 1600 100 700 500
wait 3
expect floating 101
expect floating 102
# The lid is shut: the laptop's display goes, and the monitor has its corner where the laptop's was.
quietly unplug main
move 102 160 100 700 500
wait 1.7
report-displays
wait 3
expect visible 101
expect visible 102
# The laptop alone.
quietly plug main left 1440x900
quietly make-main main
quietly unplug side
wait 1.7
report-displays
wait 3
expect at 101 60 65
expect visible 102
# Back at the desk.
quietly plug side right 1920x1080
wait 1.7
report-displays
expect at 101 60 65
expect size 101 1000x600
expect at 102 1600 100
expect size 102 700x500
wait 3
expect still
# The monitor is unplugged, and mail dragged on the lap meanwhile: it stays. Where a window is outranks what Arbor remembers.
quietly unplug side
move 102 160 100 700 500
wait 1.7
report-displays
wait 3
drag 102 700 300 quick
wait 1
quietly plug side right 1920x1080
wait 1.7
report-displays
expect still
expect at 102 350 290
expect at 101 60 65
